<title>PORTUGAL: YIELD RISES ON PORTUGUESE 3-MONTH BILLS.</title>
<headline>YIELD RISES ON PORTUGUESE 3-MONTH BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield rose slightly to 5.4661 percent, from 5.4599 percent previously, at the Institute for Public Credit Management's sale of 91-day bills, the Bank of Portugal said.</p>
<p>The Institute placed 7.1 billion escudos of the 20 billion on offer. The last such sale was on August 4.</p>
<p>--LISBON BUREAU 3511-3150035</p>
